<p>Yeah, I'm not sure about this one easier for these same reasons.</p>
<p>Honestly the only way I can think to give this any oomph would be to throw the thing in a cell deep underneath one of our storage sites where it stops moving and … who cares beyond that? Why leave it on the ocean floor when it can safely be contained on land?</p>
<p>(pls do not make it turn into super682 when you take it out of water to avoid this issue)</p>
<p>And even then that would be just another Sad Prisoner SCP, which has been done and isn't very fresh.</p>
<p>Picture's cool, living coral humanoid is cool… but it needs a gut punch in there and a bunch of logs and a demoted agent isn't doing it for me.</p>

