														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1017359">
									

<p>This just doesn't really do much for me. A little bit sad, but that's about it. SCPs need to be either creepy, very interesting, or very very witty. This is <em>slightly</em> creepy and <em>slightly</em> interesting but not enough of either to really grab me.</p>
<p>Also, why hasn't it been picked up and thrown into a containment cell somewhere to make sure it can't be moved? Leaving it out in the ocean just seems a little…silly.</p>
<p>Also, I found your tone to be just a teensy bit off. I agree with teaflower that the interview log needs work. Keep in mind that the Foundation uses empirical observations; there is no way to quantify "a feeling of warmth", so you may want to reword it with something along the lines of "agent was instructed to project feelings of warmth and welcome to SCP-496. Agent reported similar feelings returned, as well as images of whatever." Maybe better worded than that, but you get the idea.</p>
<p>So yeah, all in all a neat idea that just didn't go very far.</p>

