			<div class="content" id="post-content-1018112">
									

<p>I can see why you'd want to make it more emotionally involving, but the first version was better. This isn't really a site where you'd write up a sob story like that. You need to enhance the horror and the creep, not the heart-wrenching.</p>
<p>An idea: the statue is not intelligent enough to deduce that humans cannot survive underwater, and is so desperate for company that it will capture and drown anyone who approaches. To this end, it broadcasts a psychic 'beacon' that draws humans there to investigate, at which point they are caught and drowned.</p>
<p>Second idea: the statue is intelligent, and malevolent. The coral it is composed of can actively colonize others on contact, and convert them to a new instance. With each added instance, the statue can remain active longer when out of contact with the sea floor. Extrapolated, with enough converted humans, the group can remain active for weeks, months, years, and free to roam on dry land. Psychic beacon optional, but would probably be pushing it.</p>

